{"sections":[],"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/ivortuning\/keyboardlayout\/init(degrees:anchornote:referencenote:)"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/KeyboardLayout\/init(degrees:anchorNote:referenceNote:)"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning","doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/KeyboardLayout"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"Creates a layout whose keys are described by degrees of the tuning system, for tuning","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"systems without standard notation.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"fragments":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"degrees"},{"kind":"text","text":": ["},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int"},{"kind":"text","text":"?], "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"anchorNote"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning10NoteNumberV","text":"NoteNumber"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"referenceNote"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning10NoteNumberV","text":"NoteNumber"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning0B5ErrorO","text":"TuningError"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"title":"init(degrees:anchorNote:referenceNote:)","roleHeading":"Initializer","modules":[{"name":"IvorTuning"}],"symbolKind":"init","externalID":"s:10IvorTuning14KeyboardLayoutV7degrees10anchorNote09referenceG0ACSaySiSgG_AA0G6NumberVAJtAA0B5ErrorOYKcfc","role":"symbol"},"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"init"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"degrees"},{"text":": [","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si"},{"text":"?], ","kind":"text"},{"text":"anchorNote","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/NoteNumber","text":"NoteNumber","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning10NoteNumberV"},{"text":" = 60, ","kind":"text"},{"text":"referenceNote","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/NoteNumber","text":"NoteNumber","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning10NoteNumberV"},{"text":" = 69) ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningError","text":"TuningError","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10IvorTuning0B5ErrorO"},{"text":")","kind":"text"}],"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"kind":"parameters","parameters":[{"name":"degrees","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"One degree per key in a period, in ascending order of sound,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"wrapping at most once. ","type":"text"},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" means the key is unmapped.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The MIDI note number that sounds "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"degrees[0]"},{"type":"text","text":". Defaults to 60."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"anchorNote"},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The MIDI note number that sounds the pitch standard’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"frequency. Must fall on a mapped key. Defaults to 69."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"referenceNote"}]},{"kind":"mentions","mentions":["doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/UsingIvorTuning"]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Discussion","level":2,"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each element is the degree of the tuning system its key plays, counted from 0 (the unison)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"within one period. Key "},{"code":"anchorNote","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" sounds "},{"code":"degrees[0]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and each later mapped slot takes"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the lowest period of its degree that sounds above the previous mapped slot. Key"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"referenceNote","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" sounds the pitch standard’s frequency; the pitch standard’s pitch is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"ignored."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"degrees[0]","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" may be any degree, not only 0, and the layout need not contain degree 0 at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"all. For example, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"[5, 7, 9, 0, 2]"},{"type":"text","text":" puts degree 5 on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"anchorNote"},{"type":"text","text":", and degree 0 three keys"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"higher, in the next period."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"name":"Throws","style":"note","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":""},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorTuning\/documentation\/IvorTuning\/TuningError\/invalidKeyboardLayout(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" if "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"degrees[0]"},{"type":"text","text":" is unmapped, a degree"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is negative or appears twice, the degrees don’t ascend, or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"referenceNote"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"falls on an unmapped key."}]}],"type":"aside"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"references":{"doc://IvorTuning/documentation/IvorTuning/KeyboardLayo